    "description": "Scott Resources\nIgneous Rock Identification Kit - 15 Specimens\nProduct #2223\nThis Scott Resources igneous rock collection is a comprehensive educational tool designed for geology students and science enthusiasts. The set features 15 hand-selected specimens representing the primary textures and classifications of igneous rocks, including phaneritic, porphyritic, aphanitic (microcrystalline), and aphanitic (glassy) types.\n• 15 distinct igneous rock specimens numbered for easy identification\n• Includes descriptive identification sheet with geological definitions\n• Specimens include: Pegmatite, Granite, Granodiorite, Anorthosite, Gabbro, Monzonite Porphyry, Basalt Porphyry, Trachyte, Rhyolite, Andesite, Tuff, Obsidian, Pitchstone, Pumice, and Scoria\n• Housed in a durable maroon storage box with protective tray\nCondition:\nNew in box. The specimens are original and securely housed in their individual compartments. The identification sheet is clean and legible. The exterior storage box shows minimal shelf wear consistent with storage.",
